  "tagline": "Eclipse Foundation's Java RDF framework with native, LMDB and in-memory SPARQL stores.",
  "description": "Eclipse RDF4J, the successor to Sesame, is a Java framework for working with RDF: parsers and writers for every major format, a SPARQL 1.1 query and update engine, SHACL validation, federation (FedX), and pluggable stores including an in-memory store, the disk-based Native Store and an LMDB-backed store. RDF4J Server and Workbench expose repositories over the standard SPARQL protocol, and its SAIL API is the foundation of commercial triplestores such as GraphDB. It is the practical choice for Java teams that want an embeddable, BSD-licensed RDF store or a common API in front of several triplestores; for very large datasets, pair it with a dedicated backend.",
